<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  v465b — THE FULL EDITION'S CAMERA PERMISSION, AND ONLY THE FULL EDITION'S.

  This file is the whole reason the permission lives in a FLAVOR source set
  rather than in `main`: the ISBN scanner is a full-edition feature (the core
  edition has neither the scanner's screen nor its five CameraX / ML Kit
  dependencies), and `android.permission.CAMERA` exists for nothing else in the
  app. The v458 removal commit checked that claim before removing it — every
  other image door (an avatar, a pet, a note's photo, a gallery wall) hands the
  job to the system picker, whose camera belongs to that app, not to Curio.

  So the core edition declares NO camera permission and the Play listing shows
  no camera line for it, while the full edition restores exactly what v458 took:
  the permission, and `android.hardware.camera` as `required="false"` (a tablet
  without a camera must still be able to install, and the scanner's own
  permission gate is the screen's "Camera access is needed" state).

  AGP merges this with `app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml`, so nothing here is
  duplicated from it and nothing here is required to be complete — the merged
  result is what the full edition installs.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.CAMERA" />

    <uses-feature
        android:name="android.hardware.camera"
        android:required="false" />

</manifest>
